1. Clean up Access after centralizing Kafka producer configuration in Common
   Description
   Remove obsolete Kafka configuration and unused code from Access following the migration to Common.

Tasks
- Remove unused classes, imports, dependencies and properties.
- Update related tests and documentation.
- Keep Access-specific notification publishing logic.
  Acceptance criteria
  Access uses Common’s producer configuration, builds successfully and publishes notifications without regression.
2. Fix the Country column in the Admin SPA use-case table
   Description
   The Country column currently displays the language instead of the country.

Tasks
- Check the API response mapping and table binding.
- Display the country in the Country column and the language in the Language column.
  Acceptance criteria
  Both columns display the correct values for existing and newly created use cases.
3. Configure Dispatcher Kafka connectivity and request network access
   Description
   Prepare Dispatcher’s Kafka consumer and producer configuration, following the setup used for Access.

Tasks
- Configure bootstrap servers, input/output topics, consumer group and SSL credentials.
- Confirm the broker endpoints advertised in Kafka metadata.
- Request network access from Dispatcher pods to all required broker endpoints.
- Verify TLS connectivity, event consumption and notification publishing.
  Acceptance criteria
  Dispatcher consumes Access events and publishes Kafka notifications without connectivity, authentication or authorization errors.
4. Investigate Avro decoding in AKHQ
   Description
   Events published by Access appear as bytes in AKHQ instead of readable structured data.

Tasks
- Verify the serialization format used by Access.
- Check AKHQ’s Avro deserialization configuration and topic-to-schema mapping.
- Ensure AKHQ uses the matching schema from Common.
- Configure decoding without Schema Registry, which is currently disabled.
  Acceptance criteria
  AKHQ displays Access events as readable structured JSON, including data and metadata, without changing the event contract.

1. Fix WALLE_EUDI request endpoint in the flow without Camunda
   Description
   When using WALLE_EUDI without Camunda, the wallet calls /request/withouth-camunda/... and receives a 404 Not Found, preventing the identification flow from continuing.

Tasks
- Check the generated request URL against the controller mapping, including withouth-camunda versus without-camunda.
- Verify the endpoint is exposed correctly through the gateway.
- Correct the URL or routing and test the flow.
  Acceptance criteria
  The wallet can retrieve the request JWT and complete the identification flow without Camunda.
2. Generate dedicated DEV Kafka certificates using Horizon CLI
   Description
   Our project currently uses Kafka certificates belonging to the OBI project. Generate dedicated certificates for our services using Horizon CLI, with automated certificate lifecycle management and expiry notifications.

Tasks
- Confirm the required client/server certificate profiles with the Kafka team.
- Generate the project-specific DEV certificates through Horizon CLI.
- Prepare the required keystore and truststore, and securely store their passwords.
- Update the service configuration to replace the OBI certificates.
- Configure expiry notifications and document the renewal procedure.
  Acceptance criteria
  Our services connect to DEV Kafka using dedicated certificates, without relying on OBI certificates. Certificate expiry notifications and the renewal procedure are configured and documented
